u create a `CreditCardSuggestionGeneratorTestApi` class instead of introducing test-only methods like this? It's the pattern we usually follow.…"],["69dabc02_d58ee126",30,-18,1,"Remove"],["88d69cc0_a58a66fe",30,-18,1,"Does this need to be in the TestApi? The class' purpose is to expose private functions to the public API to allow for testing. This function seems to me like it should belong to the test fixture."],["9dcd616e_ecaf3241",17,-18,0,"Why exactly did you move this?"],["d6dcac37_8777c4e0",1,-18,1,"Bug ID"],["f18c0fe0_13405d93",30,-18,1,"Remove"],["0ae29d2a_242613e5",17,-15,1,"Can we get rid of this and instead just recompute it?"],["167d7f6c_0b7d22c5",17,-15,1,"This can also be a `raw_ref`, right?"],["2ff71db7_ae87ada8",17,-15,1,"This can also be a `raw_ref`, right?"],["63793ad1_505ebc1f",17,-15,1,"I think we can get rid of this: If we define `using VirtualCardSuggestionData = std::pair<CreditCard, std::u16string>;` then we can restrict the usage of this map to the Fetch phase."],["8c537ab0_84a87c2e",17,-15,1,"This can be a `raw_ref` right?"],["220967d7_4c907494",15,-14,1,"`&std::pair<CreditCard, std::u16string>::first`"],["41e16fa3_bbf4ef17",15,-14,1,"I don't think this was formatted correctly, it should be on the line above"],["75b05f72_14b14463",15,-14,1,"Maybe just inline? otherwise `std::move(credit_cards)`"],["a8aec895_e1b7f2bc",15,-14,1,"`for(const auto& [credit_card, virtual_card_last_four] : suggestion_data)`"],["e4ed798b_d6e5ba59",15,-14,1,"Either remove this function and inline it, or pass the map as a parameter and use it."],["39592543_2ff7a08f",15,-11,1,"This doesn't seem to be used in the function according to codesearch, but it is used in PSG, are you sure nothing is missing?"]],0,57],[7130584,20431,1627,6.284,4.514,[[3,20]],[["0bdb65e7_43fccbb0",31,-29,1,"Can we keep this called `GetCreditCardOrCvcFieldSuggestions`? There's no real need to rename it everywhere"],["185cc731_eca23135",31,-29,0,"This is duplicated, please fix"],["2d91b944_eef0a825",31,-29,1,"Any reason for modifying this? It might seem irrelevant, but changes like this make it into the blame layer, which is why when keeping some line of code as is vs. changing it has the same value, we…"],["4586ac93_bfdacc64",31,-29,1,"Why?"],["73c00f90_76713a4e",31,-29,0,"Trying to understand, how did you decide which tests to rename and which to not?"],["7ad694a3_22ecbfde",31,-29,0,"Is all of this necessary? tests should do the minimal required setup"],["88414986_59b77863",31,-29,0,"Thank you!"],["8ab8d70e_2e6affce",31,-29,1,"Why? `FieldType` is intentionally an `enum` instead of `enum class` to avoid the need to specify this everywhere."],["cd7c5b2c_b07d96c8",31,-29,1,"Why?"],["df7e9463_1542c4fd",31,-29,1,"Why was adding this necessary? The function below takes `virtual_card_guid_to_last_four_map` as a parameter. Also elsewhere"],["1305112d_beefd2b8",31,-8,1,"nit: Put the blank line after this back"],["1b1c245e_f3bc5c07",31,-8,1,"Does it, though? The four-digit combination on line 5083 is 1113, but that doesn't match the autofilled value on 5079 (unless I'm missing extra setup somewhere outside the test)"],["23eba8fc_e660e548",31,-8,1,"Please put the blank line after this back again; thanks"],["2fd13920_b68c6ecf",31,-8,1,"This is not a valid credit card number as it doesn't pass a Luhn check; please use a more standard testing value."],["6cb4c1cc_283965c5",31,-8,1,"What's the purpose of having the first four digits already entered into the field? Fields usually start blank, ya?"],["6fdcc871_b1015fa9",31,-8,1,"Should this be `Take`?"],["8d8601bf_ba8dc132",31,-8,1,"ditto"],["8ff7abf4_95817f65",31,-8,1,"nit: Period at end of sentence comment (P.S. Thank you for this comment line; it's really useful to point out where the difference lies!)"],["d8ad64e3_07d08729",31,-8,1,"Typically, if a test cares about a specific setup value, it should set up that value *in* the test. Otherwise, changes to the default setup will cause fragility with tests that for some reason…"],["e2860709_cdacd591",31,-8,1,"Ditto does not pass a Luhn check; did you mean `4444333322221111`?"]],0,58],[7245697,20432,9,0.451,0.307,[[3,21]],[],0,59],[7246656,20432,1633,6.284,4.514,[[3,22]],[],0,60],[7260954,20437,1614,6.284,4.514,[[3,22]],[],0,60],[7260541,20438,60,2.122,1.642,[[3,0.993,23,4044],[11,0.002,0,6],[12,0.001,0,4],[13,0.001,0,2],[14,0.001,0,2],[15,0.001,0,4],[2,0.001,25,2]],[["1faca343_44a8f4f5",1,-1,1,"Please mention in every CL that this CL chains follows the strategy outlined in go/ccsg-refactor-strategy and mention which step each CL is vaguely implementing."],["a6ac0d6b_1a596ccf",31,-1,0,"This should be at the top"],["f3b26fa7_7f55d396",1,0,1,"Run format in gerrit."]],0,61],[7262757,20438,51,2.122,1.642,[[3,24]],[["228a063a_69029021",1,-1,1,"ditto: Mention the strategy doc"],["3dfc538b_e2468b51",1,-1,1,"Run format in gerrit, lines should be wrapped around 80 characters"],["40bcc8cb_6178c967",32,-1,1,"the"],["4e92e7e1_1f2e0cfe",32,-1,1,"to be used for credit cards during suggestion generation."],["8c979975_91684077",32,-1,1,"CreditCard"],["a41ca4ef_98709ac4",32,-1,1,"remove"]],0,62],[7260703,20438,558,13.232,10.82,[[3,25]],[["059499d0_e6b86b72",33,-1,1,"Do we still need this?"],["0cf5b8d0_40d964b9",1,-1,1,"ditto: Mention the strategy doc"],["4f830f88_ff59c87a",1,-1,1,"of psg_util.cc"],["6687d5b5_fb4ebff3",1,-1,0,"that"],["bf387fd9_e48e9876",1,-1,1,"util"],["c04d6a5a_ae99e3c3",18,-1,1,"Let's do this in a follow up CL. The CL description mentions moving functions out of the anonymous namespace, and that's a good atomic step that should be done on its own."],["c233f5af_510e7333",1,-1,1,"header"],["c6cbcdb5_aa58f751",27,-1,1,"Do we still need this?"],["d4b4a7d1_ba6d5ab1",34,-1,0,"?"],["27616bf9_54dbd385",34,0,1,"Could you move all the functions that were removed from the anonymous namespace to the end of this file? It will make the diff cleaner."],["7f745d64_71a35a17",34,0,1,"Why are you moving those?"],["c38348df_a0eb6e2d",1,0,1,"run format on